Proposed fix: touchscreen taps are lost in LCL-gtk3 applications.

GDK_DEFAULT_EVENTS_MASK selects GDK_TOUCH_MASK on every LCL widget, which
stops X/GDK from emulating the mouse for touches, but WidgetEvent has no
GDK_TOUCH_* handling - so taps never become LCL mouse messages.

This adds GDK_TOUCH_BEGIN/UPDATE/END/CANCEL arms to TGtk3Widget.WidgetEvent.
For the pointer-emulating touch sequence (the first finger) they build the
equivalent GDK_BUTTON_PRESS / GDK_MOTION_NOTIFY / GDK_BUTTON_RELEASE event
and feed it back through WidgetEvent, so all the existing mouse handling
(focus, TButtonControl exceptions, OffsetMousePos, capture, LM_CONTEXTMENU)
applies unchanged. See ../ANALYSIS.md.

Against Lazarus main b9cfd22ae9 (2026-09-11). Applies cleanly and compiles
with FPC 3.3.1 against that tree with no errors - including every unit that
depends on gtk3widgets, since the new method changes the unit's interface
CRC. Not yet tested on touch hardware.

